{
  "version": 1,
  "status": "PROPOSED (2026-10-14). Read by nothing yet. Method: docs/BLANK_JUNK_PROPOSAL.md.",
  "notes": [
    "Matching: case-insensitive, on word boundaries, after whitespace is collapsed. 'terms' are literal phrases; 'patterns' are regexes (Python syntax).",
    "Score: UNIQUE hits. Each distinct term or pattern of a group counts once, however often it appears. group score = weight x (number of distinct terms/patterns that hit), then capped at the group's 'cap'. Overlapping phrases: the longest wins. context score = sum of its group scores. See method §4.1.",
    "weight = how much one hit is worth (1 = common, ambiguous; 2 = typical; 3-4 = nearly decisive). cap = the most one group can add, so one repeated word cannot reach a threshold alone.",
    "line_start: true means the term counts only at the start of a line (alone, or followed by ':' or '-'). Used for section headings, so 'plan' inside a sentence does not count.",
    "zone: 'any' | 'header' | 'body' | 'footer'. Header is the top 'header_band' of the page height, footer the bottom 'footer_band'. Pass 1 has no coordinates, so every zone is read as 'any' there. A junk term in the header or footer only counts when the body has at least one junk hit too.",
    "Physician names do not go here. A signed note is detected from KV extraction (Provider Signature = Yes), which runs before pass 2, and from the 'signature' group below.",
    "No 'instructions' junk group (patient instructions are clinical) and no 'insurance' demographic group (insurance wording sits on clinical, demographic and junk pages alike; it is neutral). The Instructions subtype can still come from DistilBERT."
  ],
  "thresholds": {
    "clinical": 4,
    "clinical_strong": 8,
    "junk": 4,
    "junk_strong": 7,
    "demographic": 3
  },
  "zones": {
    "header_band": 0.12,
    "footer_band": 0.08
  },
  "short_page": {
    "note": "Short page rule (precedence step R5). Content that ends within the top 'top_fraction' (15%) of the page height -> JUNK / Others, even when it carries a clinical heading and whatever the neighbouring pages are. Only exemption: Provider Signature = Yes (see method §6).",
    "top_fraction": 0.15,
    "ignore_footer_band": 0.06,
    "body_ink_band": [
      0.17,
      0.94
    ],
    "body_ink_max_fraction": 0.0001,
    "ignore_line_patterns": [
      "\\b(?:page|pg|pge)\\.?\\s*#?\\s*\\d+\\s*(?:of|/)\\s*\\d+\\b",
      "^\\s*\\d{1,4}\\s*$",
      "\\b(?:printed|print date|printed on|printed by)\\b\\s*:?\\s*\\d",
      "^\\s*(?:fax|from|to)\\b.*\\d{3}.*\\d{4}",
      "^\\s*confidential"
    ],
    "note_patterns": "A line matching any of these (anywhere in the line) is a running header / footer stamp, not content: 'Page 3 of 7', 'MRN: 023466 Printed: 10/30/2025 8:10 AM Pg 14 of 17', a bare page number, a fax transmission line."
  },
  "visual": {
    "note": "Visual = ocr_quality_results.document_type == 'visual' (CSV column document_type). Decided in pass 1 (R8): kept, or junk on very strong retrieval / invoice wording. Pass 2 is skipped for these pages. No confidence cut-off, no proxy.",
    "document_type": "visual",
    "veto_junk_groups": [
      "record_request",
      "roi_vendors",
      "invoice"
    ],
    "veto_min_score": 7
  },
